Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (primitive type variable must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (tuple of ints represents valid shape dimensions)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 9 (tensor should match size between input and mask)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 15 (tensor should be valid with respect to size)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) > 0
